Yes....it is a No Churn video, but not just any no churn video. Let's talk about some of the recipes out there (mostly bad) and also lets talk about the actual requirements for a "decent" no churn recipe. 
We are making Cookie Monster No Churn ice cream here and you will need:

400g (1 1/2 Cups) Whipping Cream
400g (10oz can) Condensed Milk
Blue food colouring
10 x Oreo cookies broken
200g (1 1/4 Cup) Cookie Dough *see below

The recipe fo rthe cookie dough is below but....you can also see it in the actual video make Salt & Straws Salted Malted Chocolate Chip Cookie Dough (epic as it is!)

Cookie Dough:
60g (1/4 cup) Unsalted Butter at room temperature
15g (1 Tbsp) Dry Malt Extract (optional but worth it)
55g (Scant 1/4 cup) Brown Sugar 
5g (1 Tsp) Salt
30ml (2 Tbsp) Cream/milk
15g (1 Tbsp) Corn Syrup
10g (2 Tsp) Vanilla Extract
90g (1/2 Cup + All-purpose 1 Tbsp)  AP Flour (Plain flour in UK) baked at 350°F (180°C) for 10 minutes to heat treat it
60g (1/3 Cup) Semi-sweet Chocolate chips

There go folks, my first functlional no churn video. I will do more if people want as this one turned out pretty decent tbh. 
